 above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:\\pi \\text{ is a rational number}$\n\n- $Q:\\pi \\text{ is a negative number}$" 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410108 1072 #uuid "e5ae3f5a-c838-553b-8c0d-d176aea1d388" 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410108 1074 "The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: \n\n$\\pi $ is a rational or negative number, \n\nwhich can be expressed symbolically as $P∨Q.$\n\nThe negation is represented by the symbol \"$¬$\".  \n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as $¬(P∨Q).$" 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410097 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410098 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410100 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410103 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1069 "q-182350" 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1071 "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1072 #uuid "f8845516-a376-50cc-8625-12673b114608" 13194139533589 17592186045417 true] [17592186410109 1074 "First, we add a column for $¬B,$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column for $B.$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $A∧¬B.$ Remember that $A∧¬B$ is true if both $A$ and $¬B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text